<command>
  <title>ArrSignedGraphical</title>
  <short_description>signed graphical arrangement</short_description>
<syntax>
ArrSignedGraphical(S: <type>RING</type>, PositiveEdgesG: <type>LIST</type>, PositiveEdgesG: <type>LIST</type>edgesG: <type>LIST</type>, loopsG: <type>LIST</type>): <rtn>LIST</rtn>
</syntax>
<description>
This function constructs the signed graphical arrangement with respect
to the list of positive edges <tt>PositiveEdgesG</tt>, of negative edges
<tt>NegativeEdgesG</tt> and of loops <tt>loopsG</tt> of the signed graph <tt>G</tt>
in the polynomial ring <tt>S</tt>.
<example>
/**/ use S::=QQ[x,y,z];	
/**/ ArrSignedGraphical(S, [[1,2],[1,3]],[[2,3]],[1,3]);
[x -y,  x -z,  y +z,  x,  z]

/**/ use S::=QQ[x[1..3]];	
/**/ ArrSignedGraphical(S, [[1,2],[1,3]],[[2,3]],[1,3]);
[x[1] -x[2],  x[1] -x[3],  x[2] +x[3],  x[1],  x[3]]
</example>
</description>
<seealso>
</seealso>
<keys>
  <key>author: palezzato, torielli</key>
</keys>
</command>
