<!-- ===  COMMAND  =============================================== -->
<command>
  <title>cyclotomic</title>
  <short_description>n-th cyclotomic polynomial</short_description>
<syntax>
cyclotomic(n: <type>INT</type>, x: <type>RINGELEM</type>): <rtn>RINGELEM</rtn>
</syntax>
<description>
This function computes the <tt>n</tt>-th cyclotomic polynomial (in the
indeterminate <tt>x</tt>).
<example>
/**/  use QQ[z];
/**/  cyclotomic(4,z);
z^2 + 1
</example>
</description>
<seealso>
  <see>CyclotomicIndex, CyclotomicTest</see>
  <see>CyclotomicFactorIndexes</see>
</seealso>
</command>
<!-- ===  COMMAND  =============================================== -->
<command>
  <title>CyclotomicFactorIndexes</title>
  <short_description>find indexes of cyclotomic factors of a polynomial</short_description>
<syntax>
CyclotomicFactorIndexes(f: <type>RINGELEM</type>): <rtn>LIST</rtn> of <rtn>INT</rtn>
CyclotomicFactors_BeukersSmyth(f: <type>RINGELEM</type>): <rtn>RECORD</rtn>
CyclotomicFactors(f: <type>RINGELEM</type>): <rtn>RECORD</rtn>
</syntax>
<description>
The function <tt>CyclotomicFactorIndexes</tt> computes a list of indexes of the
cyclotomic factors of the univariate polynomial <tt>f</tt>; it may contain some
false positives (typically 3, 4 and/or 6).
<par/>
The function <tt>CyclotomicFactors_BeukersSmyth</tt> produces a factorization of
the product of all cyclotomic factors in <tt>f</tt>; these factors are coprime.
<par/>
The function <tt>CyclotomicFactors</tt> computes the cyclotomic factors of the
univariate polynomial <tt>f</tt>; it can be slower than <tt>CyclotomicFactorIndexes</tt>.
<example>
/**/  use QQ[z];
/**/  f := (z^2+1)^2 * (z^4+z^2+1);
/**/  CyclotomicFactorIndexes(f);
[3, 4, 6]
/**/  CyclotomicFactors(f);
record[RemainingFactor:=1, factors := [z^2+z+1, z^2-z+1, z^2+1], multiplicities := [1, 1, 2]]
/**/  CyclotomicFactors_BeukersSmyth(f);
record[RemainingFactor:=1, factors := [z^4+z^2+1, z^2+1], multiplicities := [1, 2]]
</example>
</description>
<seealso>
  <see>cyclotomic</see>
  <see>CyclotomicIndex, CyclotomicTest</see>
  <see>factor</see>
</seealso>
</command>
<!-- ===  COMMAND  =============================================== -->
<command>
  <title>CyclotomicIndex, CyclotomicTest</title>
  <short_description>computes the index of a given cyclotomic polynomial</short_description>
<syntax>
CyclotomicIndex(F: <type>RINGELEM</type>): <rtn>INT</rtn>
CyclotomicTest(F: <type>RINGELEM</type>): <rtn>INT</rtn>
</syntax>
<description>
The function <tt>CyclotomicTest</tt> takes the given polynomial <tt>F</tt> and returns the
index <tt>n</tt> if it is the <tt>n</tt>-th cyclotomic polynomial; otherwise, it returns <tt>0</tt>.
To test whether a polynomial is cyclotomic, call <tt>CyclotomicTest</tt>, and
check that the result is non-zero.
<par/>
The function <tt>CyclotomicIndex</tt> is similar but faster.  It is correct if
the given polynomial is cyclotomic, but could potentially return a non-zero
value even if the input polynomial is not cyclotomic.
<example>
/**/  use R ::= QQ[x];
/**/  CyclotomicTest(x^6 +x^3 +1);
9
/**/  CyclotomicTest(x^4 -x^2 +2);
0
</example>
</description>
<seealso>
  <see>cyclotomic</see>
  <see>CyclotomicFactorIndexes</see>
</seealso>
<keys>
  <key>IsCyclotomic</key>
  <key>test for cyclotomicity</key>
</keys>
</command>
<!-- ===  end CHAPTER  =============================================== -->
</chapter_letter>
