IsOne(X: <type>OBJECT</type>): <rtn>BOOL</rtn>
</syntax>
<description>
This function tests whether its argument is one; the argument can be
of almost any type for which <em>one</em> makes sense.
<example>
/**/  IsOne(23);
false
/**/  IsOne(3/3);
true
/**/  use R ::= QQ[x,y,z];
/**/  IsOne(1);
true
/**/  IsOne(ideal(x^2, x^2-1));
true
</example>
</description>
