<command>
  <title>IsRadical</title>
  <short_description>check if an IDEAL is radical</short_description>
<syntax>
IsRadical(I: <type>IDEAL</type>): <rtn>BOOL</rtn>
</syntax>
<description>
This function tests whether the IDEAL <tt>I</tt> is radical.
Currently works only for 0-dimensional ideals.
<example>
/**/ use R ::= QQ[x,y,z];
/**/ I := ideal(x^2-1, y^2-2, z^3);
/**/ IsRadical(I);
false
/**/ I := ideal(x^2-1, y^2-2, z^3-3);
/**/ IsRadical(I);
true
</example>
</description>
<seealso>
  <see>radical</see>
  <see>IsMaximal</see>
  <see>IsPrimary</see>
</seealso>
