It returns a string containing just a newline; in CoCoA-5 it is
simpler to write <tt>\n</tt>.
<example>
/**/  str1 := "Line 1" + NewLine() + "Line 2"; --> old CoCoA-4 way
/**/  str2 := "Line 1\nLine 2";                --> more compact in CoCoA-5
/**/  str1 = str2;
true
/**/ Print str2;
Line 1
Line2
</example>
