<syntax>
tagged(E: <type>OBJECT</type>, S: <type>STRING</type>): <rtn>TAGGED(S)</rtn>
</syntax>
<description>
This function returns the object E, tagged with the string S.
Tagging is used for pretty printing of objects.  See the reference
listed below.
<example>
/**/  L := [1,2,3];
/**/  M := tagged(L,"MyTag");
/**/  type(L);
LIST

/**/  type(M);
TAGGED("$TopLevel.MyTag")

/**/  type(untagged(M));
LIST
</example>
</description>
<seealso>
  <see>Printing a Tagged Object</see>
  <see>tag</see>
  <see>untagged</see>
</seealso>
<types>
