<command>
  <title>TimeOfDay</title>
  <short_description>the current time</short_description>
<syntax>
TimeOfDay(): <rtn>INT</rtn>
</syntax>
<description>
This function returns the current time as an INT in the form
<formula>HHMMSS = HH*10000+MM*100+SS</formula> using a 24-hour clock.
<par/>
NOTE: from version 5.0.4 this information is no longer given by
the function <ttref>date</ttref>.
<example>
/**/  TimeOfDay();  -- 09:08:13
90813
/**/  date();       -- 2013-05-30
20130530
</example>
</description>
<seealso>
  <see>date</see>
</seealso>
<types>
  <type>miscellaneous</type>
</types>
</command>
